    <string name="about_campus">About Campus</string>
    <string name="about_campus_text">Located about 10 kilometers from the capital, Tunis, the University of Manouba is a public institution of higher education and scientific research distinguished by its exceptional 30-hectare campus, the only one of its kind in Tunisia.\n\nFounded in 2000, it offers a rare geographical unity that fosters interdisciplinary exchange and complementarity among fields as diverse as the humanities, social sciences, technical and experimental sciences, literature, and the arts.\n\nUMA plays a leading role in Tunisia\'s academic landscape, with a student population of 18,601 and 1,354 faculty members for the 2024–2025 academic year. It hosts several prestigious institutions, such as the Tunis Higher School of Commerce, the Higher Institute of Accounting and Business Administration (ISCAE), and the National School of Computer Science (ENSI), strengthening its national and international influence.\n\nRenowned for the quality of its academic supervision and modern facilities, the university stands out as a hub for research and innovation. It is also strongly committed to entrepreneurship, as demonstrated by its distinction in July 2024 as the leading entrepreneurial university in Africa and the MENA region.\n\nWith a high level of academic supervision and a strong interdisciplinary dynamic, the University of Manouba stands as a model of academic excellence and a driving force for innovation in Tunisia and beyond.</string>
